  "notes": "USAGE:\nAn ichidan verb often used in the te-form {秀|ひい}でている (excels, is outstanding) or as the prenominal modifier {秀|ひい}でた (outstanding, excellent). Takes the particle に to indicate the field of excellence.\n\nMore literary than {優|すぐ}れる (to be superior), which is the more common everyday equivalent.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ～に{秀|ひい}でる: to excel in...\n- {秀|ひい}でた{才能|さいのう}: outstanding talent\n- {秀|ひい}でた{能力|のうりょく}: exceptional ability\n- ひときわ{秀|ひい}でる: to stand out remarkably",
